From d7d03b13271679d76d73a69203dc3abce93bed17 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Victor Cruz <vcruz305@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 15:00:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] hc_mix: int8-weight GatedResidual decode mixer kernels
 (EXL3_GR_INT8=1)

The hyperconnection mixers (GatedResidual.fn_h / upx_h) are fp16 in an otherwise
3-bit pack: 3.2 GB resident on Qwen3.8-Flash-Next, 13.2 MB per site x 96 sites =
1.27 GB read per decode round, ~20% of the round on GB10 at ~44% of spec
bandwidth (each (M+1, R) block re-reads its weight row per stream).

Store them as int8 with per-row fp32 scales, quantized at load. gr_dots_i8 /
gr_finalize_i8 are the fp16 kernels with only the weight load changed: the scale
is constant along the contracted dim so it factors out of the k-loop, and the
fmaf chains and reduction order are byte-identical. The fp16 fused-path copies
are freed (1.6 GB back); the prefill path (proj_h / up_h) is untouched.

Measured on GB10, chat.py cold greedy 400 tok, -mtp -ndt 5 -dds -dc 0.6:
  code   74.0 -> 79.1 t/s   acceptance 73.1 -> 72.9%
  devops 55.5 -> 62.5 t/s              55.9 -> 59.2%
  prose  49.0 -> 53.0 t/s              46.1 -> 45.7%
Kernel parity vs fp32 torch on the dequantized weights: 1-2e-4 rel (mixed),
~1e-7 (post), R = 1..8. Isolated per-call 1.14-1.34x. Greedy trajectories
diverge from fp16 at token 157 / 34 / 14 (code / devops / prose); int8 was
chosen over int6 for lane-aligned loads and over int4 because a simulated int4
mixer collapsed acceptance to 20%.

Default off (EXL3_GR_INT8=1 enables) pending a second box's numbers.
